The network diagram shows the road distances, in kilometres, connecting five towns $A, B, C, D, E$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,1.4);
\coordinate (B) at (2.2,2.6);
\coordinate (C) at (2.2,0.2);
\coordinate (D) at (4.4,1.4);
\coordinate (E) at (6.4,1.4);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above left] {$11$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, below left] {$14$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$8$};
\draw (B) -- (D) node[midway, above right] {$16$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, below right] {$9$};
\draw (D) -- (E) node[midway, above] {$18$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[below] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[above] {$D$};
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt) node[right] {$E$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the total length of the path $A\text{–}C\text{–}D\text{–}E$?

A delivery vehicle leaves Depot $A$ to visit customers $B, C, D$ before returning to Depot $A$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.6);
\coordinate (B) at (3.8,2.6);
\coordinate (C) at (3.8,0);
\coordinate (D) at (0,0);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$9$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$14$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$8$};
\draw (D) -- (A) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$16$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[pos=0.25, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$18$};
\draw (B) -- (D) node[pos=0.25, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$11$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above right] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[below left] {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the total distance of the closed tour $A\text{–}B\text{–}D\text{–}C\text{–}A$?
